1
00:00:00,820 --> 00:00:02,640
Wealth, Fame, Power.

2
00:00:03,020 --> 00:00:04,557
Gold Roger, the King of the Pirates,

3
00:00:04,640 --> 00:00:07,197
attained this and everything
else the world had to offer,

4
00:00:07,280 --> 00:00:10,456
and his dying words drove
countless souls to the seas.

5
00:00:10,720 --> 00:00:11,955
You want my treasure?

6
00:00:12,180 --> 00:00:13,400
You can have it.

7
00:00:13,600 --> 00:00:16,600
I left everything I gathered
together in one place.

8
00:00:16,880 --> 00:00:19,000
Now you just have to find it.

9
00:00:20,900 --> 00:00:24,197
These words lured men to
the Grand Line in pursuit

10
00:00:24,280 --> 00:00:26,377
of dreams greater than
they'd ever dared to imagine.

11
00:00:26,460 --> 00:00:29,560
This is the time known
as the Great Pirate Era.

12
00:00:30,240 --> 00:00:35,220
Come aboard and bring along
all your hopes and dreams.

13
00:00:35,840 --> 00:00:40,620
Together we will find everything
that we're looking for.

14
00:00:41,680 --> 00:00:42,640
One Piece.

15
00:00:48,380 --> 00:00:52,517
Confess left behind,
it'll only slow us down.

16
00:00:52,600 --> 00:00:58,477
Your heart will be your guide,
raise the sails and take the helm.

17
00:00:58,560 --> 00:01:03,917
That legendary place that
the end of the map reveals.

18
00:01:04,000 --> 00:01:10,137
Is only legendary till
someone proves it real?

19
00:01:10,220 --> 00:01:14,417
Through it all, through
all the trouble of times!

20
00:01:14,500 --> 00:01:16,777
Through the heartache
and through the pain.

21
00:01:16,860 --> 00:01:21,097
Know that I will be
there and stand by you.

22
00:01:21,180 --> 00:01:24,240
Just like I know you'll stand by me.

23
00:01:25,200 --> 00:01:28,197
So come aboard and bring along.

24
00:01:28,280 --> 00:01:30,500
All your hopes and dreams.

25
00:01:31,400 --> 00:01:33,857
Together we will find everything.

26
00:01:33,940 --> 00:01:35,940
That we're looking for.

27
00:01:37,120 --> 00:01:39,657
There's always room for you.

28
00:01:39,740 --> 00:01:42,380
If you wanna be my friend!

29
00:01:43,100 --> 00:01:46,740
We are, we are on a cruise.

30
00:01:48,340 --> 00:01:49,700
We are

31
00:02:03,880 --> 00:02:04,710
Rotten woman!

32
00:02:04,960 --> 00:02:08,431
How dare you try to make a fool
of the great Captain Usopp!

33
00:02:09,300 --> 00:02:12,006
Insulting me for having
the blood of a pirate?

34
00:02:12,480 --> 00:02:14,892
Please, you don't have to do this, Usopp!

35
00:02:35,820 --> 00:02:37,340
Klahadore?

36
00:02:38,100 --> 00:02:40,100
Klahadore, are you there?

37
00:02:41,020 --> 00:02:42,840
Hello, Klahadore?

38
00:02:45,100 --> 00:02:46,700
No! Mary!

39
00:02:48,420 --> 00:02:49,420
Mary!

40
00:02:50,240 --> 00:02:51,070
Mary!

41
00:02:51,153 --> 00:02:51,983
What's going on?

42
00:02:52,066 --> 00:02:52,896
What happened to you?

43
00:02:52,979 --> 00:02:54,420
Please wake up! Mary!

44
00:02:54,920 --> 00:02:56,300
Please don't die!

45
00:02:57,300 --> 00:02:58,700
Oh, thank goodness.

46
00:02:59,080 --> 00:03:00,237
You're still alive.

47
00:03:00,320 --> 00:03:01,340
I was worried.

48
00:03:02,140 --> 00:03:02,970
Mary!

49
00:03:06,980 --> 00:03:09,520
You have to tell me who did this to you!

50
00:03:10,660 --> 00:03:12,580
Klahadore! That's who!

51
00:03:12,820 --> 00:03:14,180
He attacked me!

52
00:03:16,860 --> 00:03:17,697
He's a...

53
00:03:17,780 --> 00:03:19,060
he's a pirate!

54
00:03:19,420 --> 00:03:21,185
He's never been anything else.

55
00:03:21,740 --> 00:03:23,840
But how could that be?

56
00:03:24,520 --> 00:03:28,320
He got close to you just so
he could steal your fortune.

57
00:03:28,660 --> 00:03:30,189
That's all he ever wanted.

58
00:03:44,700 --> 00:03:48,320
And what Usopp spoke about
yesterday was the truth.

59
00:03:51,040 --> 00:03:51,880
That's right.

60
00:03:52,080 --> 00:03:53,904
And that's what is most tragic.

61
00:03:54,220 --> 00:03:58,037
When he learned the truth, he tried
his hardest to get us to hear him out.

62
00:03:58,120 --> 00:04:00,179
But we were all too shallow-minded,

63
00:04:00,380 --> 00:04:02,657
too confident in the
closed-off world we've

64
00:04:02,740 --> 00:04:05,700
lived in for so long to
listen to a single word.

65
00:04:06,580 --> 00:04:08,000
Quick! Run, Kaia!

66
00:04:08,280 --> 00:04:09,633
They're gonna kill you!

67
00:04:11,260 --> 00:04:13,848
I promise this will all
make sense tomorrow.

68
00:04:15,860 --> 00:04:19,197
In our blind protection of
the villain in our midst,

69
00:04:19,280 --> 00:04:22,977
we drove away the one brave
lad whose desperate resolve!

70
00:04:23,060 --> 00:04:27,300
he enacted for the sake and safety
of every person of this village?

71
00:04:27,560 --> 00:04:29,580
including you and I.

72
00:04:30,780 --> 00:04:32,140
Someone help!

73
00:04:32,420 --> 00:04:34,720
Mary needs help! No, miss.

74
00:04:34,920 --> 00:04:36,340
It's of no use.

75
00:04:38,220 --> 00:04:40,900
The entire staff is on leave.

76
00:04:41,160 --> 00:04:43,336
No one has been here since yesterday.

77
00:04:44,420 --> 00:04:45,250
What?

78
00:04:45,333 --> 00:04:46,163
Then I just...

79
00:04:46,246 --> 00:04:47,076
I'll find...

80
00:04:47,159 --> 00:04:49,437
You cannot let yourself
get flustered, miss.

81
00:04:49,520 --> 00:04:51,740
We know the attack has yet to begin,

82
00:04:51,980 --> 00:04:56,360
so be calm and think clearly about
what it is you have to do next.

83
00:04:58,740 --> 00:05:02,077
Because if Klahadore is the
thief we understand him to be,

84
00:05:02,160 --> 00:05:06,577
and his goal is your fortune and your
mansion, then by all means let him have it.

85
00:05:06,660 --> 00:05:09,542
None of this is worth
sacrificing your life over.

86
00:05:12,180 --> 00:05:13,010
Yes.

87
00:05:13,280 --> 00:05:18,480
It's a cruel truth, but you are the only
one who can stop Clawador now, Kaya.

88
00:05:20,260 --> 00:05:21,460
Can you do it?

89
00:05:21,680 --> 00:05:25,400
I know this is not your
burden, but still I must ask.

90
00:05:25,940 --> 00:05:28,520
Yes, I understand, and I will do it.

91
00:05:28,860 --> 00:05:31,389
This isn't a situation
I can run away from.

92
00:05:31,680 --> 00:05:34,160
I know what consequences I face.

93
00:05:34,780 --> 00:05:37,800
I will find Clawador
and I will finish this.

94
00:05:41,720 --> 00:05:42,550
What?

95
00:05:42,700 --> 00:05:44,935
You saw Clawador heading to the shore?

96
00:05:45,400 --> 00:05:48,459
Yeah, and he had this weird,
scary look on his face.

97
00:05:50,080 --> 00:05:51,609
Carrot, would you wake up?

98
00:05:52,860 --> 00:05:55,280
Come on, it's way too early for this.

99
00:05:55,720 --> 00:05:57,426
This is no time for laziness.

100
00:05:57,640 --> 00:06:00,287
Horrible things could
be happening right now.

101
00:06:02,820 --> 00:06:05,597
I still think the pirates
are going to attack soon.

102
00:06:05,680 --> 00:06:10,237
I know our captain said that was a lie,
but I think he was the one that was lying.

103
00:06:10,320 --> 00:06:11,967
Yeah, you're probably right.

104
00:06:12,700 --> 00:06:13,530
It was weird.

105
00:06:13,640 --> 00:06:14,897
He seemed off yesterday.

106
00:06:14,980 --> 00:06:16,757
The captain wasn't his usual self.

107
00:06:16,840 --> 00:06:17,670
It's Kaya.

108
00:06:17,820 --> 00:06:18,761
She's all right.

109
00:06:30,240 --> 00:06:32,937
Looks like something's
got her really bothered.

110
00:06:33,020 --> 00:06:36,491
Yeah, walking around outside
by herself doesn't seem right.

111
00:06:36,600 --> 00:06:37,835
Something's going on.

112
00:06:38,420 --> 00:06:40,220
Something really weird.

113
00:06:43,860 --> 00:06:46,380
Come forth, Meowban brothers!

114
00:06:50,560 --> 00:06:51,540
Yes, Captain?

115
00:06:51,800 --> 00:06:53,100
Did you call for us?

116
00:06:54,920 --> 00:06:56,000
Well, did you?

117
00:06:57,080 --> 00:06:58,580
Xiong! And Bucci!

118
00:06:59,140 --> 00:07:01,375
Together we are the Meowban brothers!

119
00:07:01,560 --> 00:07:02,501
At your service!

120
00:07:06,020 --> 00:07:06,850
Bucci,

121
00:07:06,933 --> 00:07:09,460
Xiong, we absolutely
must get up this hill,

122
00:07:09,560 --> 00:07:11,537
but as you can plainly
see, our path is blocked.

123
00:07:11,620 --> 00:07:15,497
What if he would be so kind as to
remove this obstacle immediately?

124
00:07:15,580 --> 00:07:16,880
Hey! No way!

125
00:07:17,100 --> 00:07:18,237
We couldn't do that!

126
00:07:18,320 --> 00:07:19,496
He looks too strong!

127
00:07:19,740 --> 00:07:20,720
Right, Bucci?

128
00:07:21,140 --> 00:07:22,540
Oh, yeah, he's strong.

129
00:07:22,720 --> 00:07:23,955
Way stronger than us.

130
00:07:24,300 --> 00:07:25,130
Huh?

131
00:07:25,860 --> 00:07:28,801
Besides, we just guard the
ship, not fight people!

132
00:07:29,060 --> 00:07:30,060
He's got a point.

133
00:07:30,240 --> 00:07:33,117
We're really not the guys
you want to send into battle.

134
00:07:33,200 --> 00:07:35,082
So, they're a couple of pansies.

135
00:07:35,260 --> 00:07:37,737
I guess they're not the
trump card after all.

136
00:07:37,820 --> 00:07:42,300
Xiong, just do it already! Ah!
What? Please, not me! And hurry!

137
00:07:42,680 --> 00:07:44,820
Okay, I'll go. Just stop yelling.

138
00:07:45,300 --> 00:07:47,006
The guy's crying like a baby.

139
00:07:47,200 --> 00:07:49,024
What are they doing down there?

140
00:07:50,320 --> 00:07:53,160
Of all people, why force
that guy into a fight?

141
00:07:53,260 --> 00:07:54,437
I'm gonna tear you off with these claws!

142
00:07:54,520 --> 00:07:55,717
You just wait and see!

143
00:07:55,800 --> 00:07:58,537
I'm a vicious killing machine,
and I'm coming for you!

144
00:07:58,620 --> 00:07:59,502
You bad people!

145
00:07:59,820 --> 00:08:02,526
You come any closer, and
I'll cut you in half!

146
00:08:02,920 --> 00:08:04,060
I'm not joking!

147
00:08:04,260 --> 00:08:05,100
I'll do it!

148
00:08:07,160 --> 00:08:08,120
Not likely.

149
00:08:13,420 --> 00:08:15,100
Impressed? Too bad.

150
00:08:15,800 --> 00:08:18,220
It seems you fell for my little ruse.

151
00:08:18,700 --> 00:08:23,288
I'm impressed you blocked me, considering
what a brilliant performance I gave.

152
00:08:23,760 --> 00:08:26,257
Don't let the teeny bit
of skill you have cause

153
00:08:26,340 --> 00:08:29,281
you to underestimate Siam
of the Meowpad Brothers.

154
00:08:33,480 --> 00:08:35,009
Are you missing something?

155
00:08:35,180 --> 00:08:37,533
Not that I would know anything about it.

156
00:08:38,500 --> 00:08:39,440
There it is.

157
00:08:39,560 --> 00:08:45,940
Cat burglar give me my swords back your
swords, but you already have a sword.

158
00:08:46,060 --> 00:08:47,354
How greedy can you be?

159
00:08:50,700 --> 00:08:52,220
Say goodbye swords.

160
00:08:52,400 --> 00:08:53,230
Goodbye

161
00:09:01,320 --> 00:09:03,400
Now I feel lighter

162
00:09:14,620 --> 00:09:18,480
You really have to be faster,
because I'm agile as a cat.

163
00:09:23,800 --> 00:09:25,980
Beach, you're up. Get in here.

164
00:09:26,280 --> 00:09:27,280
She makes you up.

165
00:09:33,820 --> 00:09:34,820
Faster, buddy!

166
00:09:37,880 --> 00:09:38,920
Damn, Beach!

167
00:09:39,180 --> 00:09:40,415
He got away from you!

168
00:09:40,820 --> 00:09:43,357
Now he's right there, and
I'll hold him tight this time!

169
00:09:43,440 --> 00:09:44,675
Careful, he's strong.

170
00:09:44,860 --> 00:09:47,857
Stronger than I thought he'd
be, even without all his blades.

171
00:09:47,940 --> 00:09:50,058
This is getting worse by the second.

172
00:09:50,660 --> 00:09:55,131
If Tummy there would have landed on me,
I'd have been pounded into the dust.

173
00:09:55,440 --> 00:09:57,137
We'll get him for sure this time!

174
00:09:57,220 --> 00:09:58,338
You got that right!

175
00:09:58,640 --> 00:10:02,287
One sword technique's not my
forte, fellas, but what the hell?

176
00:10:02,900 --> 00:10:04,940
Let's go, Bootsie!

177
00:10:05,200 --> 00:10:07,160
Right, Siam, let's do it!

178
00:10:07,560 --> 00:10:09,440
Pussy with an old moth!

179
00:10:17,820 --> 00:10:18,920
This isn't good!

180
00:10:19,200 --> 00:10:20,965
They got him on the defensive!

181
00:10:23,640 --> 00:10:25,111
What are you doing, Usam?

182
00:10:25,280 --> 00:10:27,397
There's no way that
Zoro can gain any ground

183
00:10:27,480 --> 00:10:29,377
if he's too busy blocking their attacks!

184
00:10:29,460 --> 00:10:30,578
I'm gonna help him!

185
00:10:30,860 --> 00:10:31,980
Take this!

186
00:10:33,000 --> 00:10:33,830
Let's go!

187
00:10:40,000 --> 00:10:41,400
This is our chance!

188
00:10:47,060 --> 00:10:49,857
You're supposed to shoot
at the bad guys, you idiot!

189
00:10:49,940 --> 00:10:50,860
But I did!

190
00:10:52,200 --> 00:10:53,057
It was...

191
00:10:53,140 --> 00:10:55,817
it was like he moved in
front of my shot on purpose!

192
00:10:55,900 --> 00:10:57,371
But why would he do that?

193
00:10:59,780 --> 00:11:01,640
You dumbass! Don't help me!

194
00:11:01,920 --> 00:11:02,861
You want to die?

195
00:11:07,280 --> 00:11:11,700
It's just a thought, but maybe it's
the two of us who just got saved.

196
00:11:12,140 --> 00:11:16,097
If you had actually hit one of those guys,
they would have come after us instead.

197
00:11:16,180 --> 00:11:19,827
Then we wouldn't have had a
chance of holding up against that.

198
00:11:20,720 --> 00:11:21,550
What a guy.

199
00:11:21,633 --> 00:11:23,914
All this time, he was worried about us.

200
00:11:27,360 --> 00:11:30,536
If I just had one more sword,
I could take these guys.

201
00:11:32,940 --> 00:11:34,317
I'm gonna get the swords.

202
00:11:34,400 --> 00:11:37,917
If I can get them back to Zoro,
there'll be no way he can lose.

203
00:11:38,000 --> 00:11:39,300
Let me get the swords.

204
00:11:40,400 --> 00:11:41,576
Don't push yourself.

205
00:11:41,780 --> 00:11:44,192
You can barely even stand up on your own.

206
00:11:45,460 --> 00:11:46,290
Nubby!

207
00:11:57,360 --> 00:11:58,190
Huuu!

208
00:12:06,360 --> 00:12:07,220
Nami!

209
00:12:08,160 --> 00:12:09,807
What do you need swords for?

210
00:12:23,960 --> 00:12:24,820
No!

211
00:12:25,300 --> 00:12:26,130
I'm sorry!

212
00:12:26,213 --> 00:12:28,920
I can explain all of this!

213
00:12:34,140 --> 00:12:36,920
The night has long since passed.

214
00:12:37,400 --> 00:12:43,700
So why is it that you seem to have made
no progress on the plan? Captain! No!

215
00:12:44,820 --> 00:12:46,280
He'll kill us all!

216
00:12:52,640 --> 00:12:54,000
It's all over.

217
00:13:07,740 --> 00:13:10,640
What the hell is going on?

218
00:13:16,240 --> 00:13:19,320
To think that these
brats have held you back.

219
00:13:20,400 --> 00:13:23,320
How the black cat pirates have fallen.

220
00:13:24,160 --> 00:13:26,395
What have you got to say for yourself?

221
00:13:27,100 --> 00:13:27,930
Jungle!

222
00:13:32,540 --> 00:13:35,137
But, uh, well, I...

223
00:13:35,220 --> 00:13:36,797
You said...

224
00:13:36,880 --> 00:13:41,500
Sorry, sir, but you said letting the
kid go wouldn't cause any problems.

225
00:13:44,460 --> 00:13:45,960
I did say that.

226
00:13:47,520 --> 00:13:48,477
What's your point?

227
00:13:48,560 --> 00:13:49,460
He's an idiot.

228
00:13:49,760 --> 00:13:51,857
I knew no one would listen
to his warnings and he

229
00:13:51,940 --> 00:13:54,677
would come stumbling back
to take a stand against us.

230
00:13:54,760 --> 00:14:00,100
But the one thing I hadn't taken account
for was your inexcusable weakness.

231
00:14:01,080 --> 00:14:02,180
We're not weak.

232
00:14:02,440 --> 00:14:03,637
It's just that...

233
00:14:03,720 --> 00:14:05,977
Who are you to call us weak?

234
00:14:06,060 --> 00:14:08,001
What would you say, Captain Kuro?

235
00:14:10,200 --> 00:14:12,340
You used to be quite the killer.

236
00:14:12,860 --> 00:14:15,337
But face it, kuro, it's been three years!

237
00:14:15,420 --> 00:14:17,857
and we haven't exactly
been living the good life?

238
00:14:17,940 --> 00:14:20,116
waiting on a rich girl hand and foot.

239
00:14:20,400 --> 00:14:21,660
Yeah, that's right.

240
00:14:21,820 --> 00:14:26,644
For three long years, we've been out sinking
pirate ships and massacring villages.

241
00:14:28,100 --> 00:14:30,600
Very good. Finished. No!

242
00:14:30,880 --> 00:14:32,697
You've done nothing this whole time!

243
00:14:32,780 --> 00:14:34,300
We've been killing you!

244
00:14:34,520 --> 00:14:37,873
Butler, there's no way you
can beat the Mialban brothers!

245
00:14:41,800 --> 00:14:44,160
Don't! Bucci! Xion! Stop!

246
00:14:49,780 --> 00:14:52,040
YOU ARE NOT CAPTAIN ANYMORE!

247
00:14:52,980 --> 00:14:55,580
So sorry, but we have to kill you!

248
00:15:07,880 --> 00:15:09,460
What? He's behind him!

249
00:15:09,640 --> 00:15:10,677
How the hell'd he...

250
00:15:10,760 --> 00:15:12,584
I'm one of those crazy weapons.

251
00:15:13,260 --> 00:15:15,160
Who are you going to kill?

252
00:15:17,600 --> 00:15:20,460
He snuck out right behind us!

253
00:15:26,500 --> 00:15:27,780
He's gone!

254
00:15:30,500 --> 00:15:33,080
The Pussyfoot Maneuver!

255
00:15:37,880 --> 00:15:39,920
You know, you're right.

256
00:15:45,160 --> 00:15:48,277
I do feel a bit sluggish
after all these years.

257
00:15:48,360 --> 00:15:52,737
He's handling them like
babies and those two

258
00:15:52,820 --> 00:15:57,497
nearly defeated Zoro with
his pussyfoot maneuver.

259
00:15:57,580 --> 00:16:02,197
Captain Kuro could shred everyone on this
beach before we drew our next breath.

260
00:16:02,280 --> 00:16:05,037
We wouldn't even see it coming.

261
00:16:05,120 --> 00:16:08,897
There is no escape from a
killing machine like him.

262
00:16:08,980 --> 00:16:15,437
